From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] DwUsbHostDxe: support the BCM2712 DWC2 OTG (Pi 5 USB-C)

The Pi 5's USB-C data lines are wired to the same Synopsys DWC2 OTG core
the Pi 0-3 used ("brcm,bcm2835-usb" in the firmware DTB), relocated from
the BCM283x legacy peripheral window to the main AXI bus at
0x10'0048'0000 (/axi/usb@480000, identity-mapped, per the firmware DTB
and its dwc2.dtbo overlay symbols). Three changes make the existing
driver work there:

1. Base address from a new 64-bit PcdDwUsbBaseAddress (same pattern as
   the RPi5 port's PcdFwMailboxBaseAddress / PcdBcm2838RngBaseAddress).
   Zero - the default - selects the legacy BCM2836_USB_BASE_ADDRESS, so
   Pi 3/4 builds are unchanged.

2. Force host mode at the end of core init. The Pi 3 straps the OTG ID
   pin to host; on the Pi 5 the core samples as a device out of reset
   (the boot ROM's rpiboot gadget runs on it), and Linux only gets a
   host on this port by forcing dr_mode = "host". Forcing is a no-op
   where the ID strap already selects host.

3. The VideoCore SetPowerState (USB HCD) mailbox call is best-effort
   instead of fatal: on BCM2712 the block is powered and clocked from
   reset and the firmware may not implement that device id.

The platform must also give the controller correct DMA parameters: on
BCM2712 the DWC2 masters the AXI bus identity-mapped (no 0xC000_0000
legacy alias), with 32-bit DMA address registers - RPi5.dsc scopes
PcdDmaDeviceOffset|0 and a below-4GB limit onto this driver.

Upstream-Status: Submittable [with an RPi5 platform port]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DriverBinding.c b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DriverBinding.c
index bb228e6..fc901d7 100644
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DriverBinding.c
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DriverBinding.c
@@ -125,10 +125,16 @@ DriverStart (
     return Status;
   }
 
+  //
+  // Best-effort: the VideoCore mailbox implements this power domain on
+  // BCM283x/BCM2711, but on BCM2712 the DWC2 block is powered and
+  // clocked from reset (the boot ROM's rpiboot gadget runs on it) and
+  // the firmware may not implement the USB HCD device id, so a mailbox
+  // refusal must not veto the host controller.
+  //
   Status = mFwProtocol->SetPowerState (RPI_MBOX_POWER_STATE_USB_HCD, TRUE, TRUE);
   if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
-    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "Couldn't power on USB: %r\n", Status));
-    return Status;
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "Couldn't power on USB: %r (continuing)\n", Status));
   }
 
   Status = CreateDwUsbHc (&DwHc);
diff --git a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
index 0cd833c..e97c1c3 100644
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
@@ -1448,6 +1448,16 @@ DwCoreInit (
   MmioWrite32 (DwHc->DwUsbBase + GAHBCFG, AhbCfg);
   MmioAnd32 (DwHc->DwUsbBase + GUSBCFG, ~(DWC2_GUSBCFG_HNPCAP | DWC2_GUSBCFG_SRPCAP));
 
+  //
+  // Force host mode. The Pi 3 straps the OTG ID pin to host, but on the
+  // Pi 5 this core sits behind the USB-C connector and samples as a
+  // device out of reset (the boot ROM's rpiboot gadget runs on it), so
+  // without the force a connected peripheral is never seen. The Synopsys
+  // core is allowed up to 25 ms to effect a mode change.
+  //
+  MmioOr32 (DwHc->DwUsbBase + GUSBCFG, DWC2_GUSBCFG_FORCEHOSTMODE);
+  MicroSecondDelay (25000);
+
   return EFI_SUCCESS;
 }
 
@@ -1587,7 +1597,15 @@ CreateDwUsbHc (
   DwHc->DwUsbOtgHc.ClearRootHubPortFeature        = DwHcClearRootHubPortFeature;
   DwHc->DwUsbOtgHc.MajorRevision                  = 0x02;
   DwHc->DwUsbOtgHc.MinorRevision                  = 0x00;
-  DwHc->DwUsbBase                                 = BCM2836_USB_BASE_ADDRESS;
+  //
+  // PcdDwUsbBaseAddress carries the controller base on SoCs whose DWC2
+  // is not at the BCM283x legacy offset (BCM2712: 0x10'0048'0000). Zero
+  // selects the legacy BCM283x address, keeping Pi 3/4 unchanged.
+  //
+  DwHc->DwUsbBase                                 = FixedPcdGet64 (PcdDwUsbBaseAddress);
+  if (DwHc->DwUsbBase == 0) {
+    DwHc->DwUsbBase                               = BCM2836_USB_BASE_ADDRESS;
+  }
 
   Pages = EFI_SIZE_TO_PAGES (DWC2_STATUS_BUF_SIZE);
   DwHc->StatusBuffer = AllocatePages (Pages);
diff --git a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.inf b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.inf
index 8817f20..0f255ba 100644
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.inf
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.inf
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@
 
 [FixedPcd]
   gBcm283xTokenSpaceGuid.PcdBcm283xRegistersAddress
+  gRaspberryPiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdDwUsbBaseAddress
 
 [Depex]
   gRaspberryPiFirmwareProtocolGuid
diff --git a/Platform/RaspberryPi/RaspberryPi.dec b/Platform/RaspberryPi/RaspberryPi.dec
index 5c050f8..dd560f3 100644
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/RaspberryPi.dec
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/RaspberryPi.dec
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@
   gRaspberryPiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdGicPmuIrq2|0x0|UINT32|0x00000035
   gRaspberryPiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdGicPmuIrq3|0x0|UINT32|0x00000036
   gRaspberryPiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdFwMailboxBaseAddress|0x0|UINT64|0x00000037
+  gRaspberryPiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdDwUsbBaseAddress|0x0|UINT64|0x00000038
 
 [PcdsFixedAtBuild, PcdsPatchableInModule, PcdsDynamic, PcdsDynamicEx]
   gRaspberryPiTokenSpaceGuid.PcdCpuClock|0|UINT32|0x0000000d
